#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:1
msgid "TileLang Metal Backend Internals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:3
msgid ""
"This document explains how the TileLang Metal backend lowers a TileLang "
"kernel to Metal shader source, how the current GEMM fast path is "
"implemented, which backend work does not map one-to-one to CUDA, and where "
"the next optimization work should land."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:8
msgid ""
"This is not an Apple GPU architecture overview or a TileLang frontend "
"tutorial. Metal and Apple GPU background is introduced only where it affects "
"lowering, codegen, runtime behavior, or performance policy. Reference "
"material is grouped in Section 5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:13
msgid "How to read this document:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:15
msgid "To understand the current fast path, read Section 0 and Section 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:16
msgid ""
"To work on the Metal backend or codegen, read Sections 1, 2, and 3, then use "
"Section 5 as reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:18
msgid "To write TileLang kernels for Metal, read Section 0 and Section 4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:19
msgid ""
"To find performance data, implementation files, or test commands, go to "
"Section 5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:22
msgid "0. TL;DR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:24
msgid ""
"The current default fast path is **direct-global cooperative tensor**: A/B "
"are loaded from `device` memory without `threadgroup` staging, C accumulates "
"in a cooperative tensor destination, and the result is stored back to global "
"C."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:27
msgid ""
"Default benchmark configuration: `ct_global`, `block_M=64`, `block_N=128`, "
"`threads=128` (4 simdgroups), fp16 input, fp16 output, fp32 accumulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:29
msgid ""
"On the current full-tile fp16 GEMM snapshot, TileLang is at or slightly "
"above MLX and about 5-6% behind PyTorch MPS. See Section 5.6."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:31
msgid ""
"The most important mental model: **Metal is not CUDA**. On Apple unified "
"memory, `gmem -> smem` is not a performance hint. Shared staging should be "
"preserved when it carries real semantics such as layout, padding, or reuse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:34
msgid ""
"The other paths, shared cooperative tensor and simdgroup, still exist for "
"compatibility and semantic coverage. They are not the current performance "
"mainline. See Section 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:38
msgid "1. The Fast Path, End to End"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:40
msgid ""
"This section traces one concrete direct-global cooperative tensor kernel "
"from TileLang source to generated MSL and then to the performance snapshot. "
"Later sections explain the mechanisms behind this path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:44
msgid "1.1 The Kernel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:46
msgid ""
"with T.Kernel(T.ceildiv(N, block_N), T.ceildiv(M, block_M), threads=128) as "
"(bx, by):\n"
"    T.gemm(\n"
"        A[by * block_M:(by + 1) * block_M, 0:K],\n"
"        B[0:K, bx * block_N:(bx + 1) * block_N],\n"
"        C[by * block_M:(by + 1) * block_M, bx * block_N:(bx + 1) * "
"block_N],\n"
"        clear_accum=True,\n"
"    )\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:56
msgid ""
"A, B, and C are all tile views over `global` tensors. There is no "
"`alloc_shared`, no `T.copy` staging, and no handwritten K-loop. For full-"
"tile GEMM, the backend expands the K reduction during lowering. This is the "
"intended frontend shape: express operand regions and dtypes, and let the "
"backend own lane mapping, operand construction, and accumulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:62
msgid "1.2 Path Selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:64
msgid ""
"When the backend sees this `T.gemm`, the instruction selection and Metal "
"GEMM lowering logic pick the direct-global cooperative tensor path. The "
"detailed selection rules are in Section 2.1. For this kernel, A/B are "
"`global`, C is not shared, and the tile shape and thread count allow "
"cooperative tensor lowering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:69
msgid "For `M=128, N=256, K=128, block_M=64, block_N=128, threads=128`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:71
msgid "`threads=128` means 4 simdgroups."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:72
msgid "The 4 simdgroups cover a `64 x 128` C tile as a `2 x 2` partition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:73
msgid "Each simdgroup owns a `32 x 64` C sub-tile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:74
msgid ""
"Each `32 x 64` sub-tile is covered by `(32 / 16) x (64 / 32) = 4` op-level "
"fragments, corresponding to 4 destination cooperative tensors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:77
msgid "1.3 The MPP op: `matmul2d(M, N, K)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:79
msgid "The core operation is an MPP tensor op. The generated MSL contains:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:81
msgid ""
"constexpr auto __pct_desc = mpp::tensor_ops::matmul2d_descriptor(\n"
"    16, 32, 16, /*trans_a=*/false, /*trans_b=*/false, /*accumulate=*/true,\n"
"    mpp::tensor_ops::matmul2d_descriptor::mode::multiply_accumulate);\n"
"mpp::tensor_ops::matmul2d<__pct_desc, metal::execution_simdgroup> __pct_op;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:88
msgid ""
"In this document, `matmul2d(M, N, K)` refers to the first three shape "
"parameters of the descriptor, in M / N / K order. A single MPP op produces "
"an `M x N` destination fragment and reduces along K. These parameters are "
"not TileLang `block_M` / `block_N`, and they are not the whole threadgroup "
"tile shape. The current fast path specializes to `matmul2d(16, 32, 16)`. "
"Larger simdgroup and threadgroup tiles are covered by multiple op-level "
"fragments, such as the 4 destination cooperative tensors above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:96
msgid "1.4 The Generated MSL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:98
msgid ""
"The following is a representative snippet for the shape above. Repeated "
"fragments are omitted for readability. It is generated with `accum_dtype=T."
"float16`, so C is `device half*` and the final store contains a `half4(...)` "
"cast. Existing codegen tests use `accum_dtype=T.float32` by default, which "
"generates `device float* C` and no fp32-to-fp16 store cast. To reproduce "
"this fp16-output source exactly, pass `accum_dtype=T.float16`; see Section "
"5.8."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:105
msgid "Kernel signature and execution attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:107
msgid ""
"[[kernel, max_total_threads_per_threadgroup(128)]] void main_kernel(\n"
"    const device half* __restrict A [[ buffer(0) ]],\n"
"    const device half* __restrict B [[ buffer(1) ]],\n"
"    device half* __restrict C [[ buffer(2) ]],\n"
"    uint3 blockIdx [[threadgroup_position_in_grid]],\n"
"    uint3 __gridDim [[threadgroups_per_grid]],\n"
"    uint3 threadIdx [[thread_position_in_threadgroup]],\n"
"    uint __simd_group_id [[simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup]]) {\n"
"  const ushort __lane = __metal_get_thread_index_in_simdgroup(ushort());\n"
"  ...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:120
msgid ""
"Destination cooperative tensors are created and zeroed before the K-loop. C "
"storage is elided: C does not round-trip through a `thread` array and "
"instead persists in cooperative tensor destination objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:124
msgid ""
"auto __pct_c0 = __pct_op.get_destination_cooperative_tensor<...>();\n"
"// __pct_c1 / __pct_c2 / __pct_c3 are created the same way.\n"
"TILELANG_PRAGMA_UNROLL for (ushort __i = 0; __i < 16; __i++) __pct_c0[__i] = "
"0.0f;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:130
msgid ""
"Inside the K-loop, A/B are loaded from `device` memory into thread-private "
"temporary storage and then moved into MPP cooperative tensor operands. There "
"is no `threadgroup` allocation and no barrier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:134
msgid ""
"for (int k_outer = 0; k_outer < 8; ++k_outer) {\n"
"  const device half* __src =\n"
"      (const device half*)(&(A[((blockIdx.y * 8192) +\n"
"                                ((__simd_group_id & 1) * 4096)) +\n"
"                               (k_outer * 16)]));\n"
"  // half4 vector loads into A_local ...\n"
"  // B loads follow the same pattern ...\n"
"  auto __ct_a = __pct_op.get_left_input_cooperative_tensor<half, half, "
"float>();\n"
"  auto __ct_b = __pct_op.get_right_input_cooperative_tensor<half, half, "
"float>();\n"
"  // A_local / B_local -> __ct_a / __ct_b\n"
"  __pct_op.run(__ct_a, __ct_b, __pct_c0);  // fp32 accumulation\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:149
msgid ""
"After the K-loop, C is stored. For fp16 output, the fp32 destination values "
"are cast on store:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:152
msgid ""
"device half* __dst = (device half*)(&(C[...]));\n"
"*(device half4*)(&__dst[__r0 * 256 + __c0]) =\n"
"    half4(*(thread float4*)(&__pct_c0[0]));\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:158
msgid "Important source-shape properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:160
msgid ""
"A/B are `const device half* __restrict`; C is `device half* __restrict`. "
"This preserves read-only and noalias information for the Metal compiler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:162
msgid ""
"simdgroup id and lane id come from Metal execution attributes "
"(`__simd_group_id`, `__metal_get_thread_index_in_simdgroup`) instead of "
"being repeatedly derived from `threadIdx`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:165
msgid ""
"Addresses have the shape `base + tile offset + simdgroup offset + K-loop "
"induction`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:167
msgid ""
"`mpp::...matmul2d` destinations accumulate in fp32; fp16 output is handled "
"at store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:169
msgid "There is no `threadgroup half` declaration and no barrier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:171
msgid "1.5 Why This Is Not a CUDA Translation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:173
msgid ""
"This path is not a step-by-step translation of the common CUDA `global -> "
"shared -> ldmatrix -> mma` pipeline:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:176
msgid ""
"CUDA:  device A/B -> shared -> ldmatrix -> mma -> shared/reg -> device C\n"
"Metal: device A/B ------------> MPP operand -> matmul2d -> destination CT -> "
"device C\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:181
msgid ""
"The Metal backend chooses a source shape that matches MPP directly. On Apple "
"unified memory, moving A/B through `threadgroup` before feeding the tensor "
"op is usually an extra copy and barrier when it carries no semantic value. "
"This is why the shared path in Section 3 is correct but slower for the "
"current full-tile GEMM snapshot."
msgstr ""

