#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:239
msgid "2.2 Surrounding Lowering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:241
msgid ""
"The launch, allocation, loop, copy, and swizzle lowering around GEMM "
"determine what source shape the intrinsic sequence sits in. For the direct-"
"global path:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:244
msgid ""
"**Launch**: `T.Kernel(..., threads=N)` lowers to a Metal threadgroup launch, "
"emitting `max_total_threads_per_threadgroup(N)`, `blockIdx` / `threadIdx` "
"style indices, simdgroup id, and lane id. Matrix work is still partitioned "
"by 32-lane simdgroups; there is no CUDA WGMMA-style 128-thread warpgroup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:248
msgid ""
"**Allocation**: the direct-global path does not allocate `threadgroup` "
"buffers. A/B use `thread` temporary arrays. C persists in `metal."
"cooperative_tensor` destination objects when storage elision applies. The "
"full scope-to-object mapping is in Section 5.2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:252
msgid ""
"**Loop**: the K-loop generates affine addresses of the form `base + tile "
"offset + simdgroup offset + K-loop induction`. It does not rely on CUDA-"
"style software pipelining or make shared staging the inner-loop policy. "
"Pointer induction and address hoisting remain optimization targets (Section "
"5.5)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:257
msgid ""
"**Copy / sync**: the direct-global path is device load/store plus MPP "
"operand construction. With no shared dataflow, it avoids threadgroup copy "
"and barrier operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:260
msgid ""
"**Swizzle**: block-level swizzle is supported. `T.use_swizzle(panel_size, "
"order=\"mlx\")` maps to `rasterization2DMLX`, canonicalizing physical block "
"index to logical tile index and avoiding repeated physical-index arithmetic "
"in generated MSL. This is block/grid-level swizzle, not CUDA-style thread-"
"level or per-thread swizzle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:266
msgid "2.3 Metal-Specific Work (No CUDA Counterpart)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:268
msgid ""
"The direct-global path includes backend work that does not have a direct "
"CUDA counterpart:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:271
msgid ""
"**Direct-global cooperative tensor lowering**: A/B become MPP operands from "
"`device` memory without explicit shared staging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:273
msgid ""
"**Cooperative tensor destination management**: C accumulates in MPP "
"destination objects; small C cooperative tensor storage can elide a thread-"
"local array (Section 1.4)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:276
msgid ""
"**fp16 output / fp32 accumulation split**: MPP destinations use fp32, and "
"the store to fp16 C performs the cast."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:278
msgid ""
"**MLX-style block rasterization**: physical block indices are canonicalized "
"to logical tile indices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:280
msgid ""
"**simdgroup id / lane id lowering**: Metal execution attributes are used "
"instead of re-deriving them from thread id."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:282
msgid ""
"**Metal 4 target capability gate**: cooperative tensor lowering requires the "
"`metal4` target key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:284
msgid ""
"**Metal 4 runtime language-version guard**: MSL 4.0 is requested only when "
"the SDK, runtime OS, and device family support it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:287
msgid ""
"This work is closer to Metal backend canonicalization and source-shape "
"construction than to mechanical CUDA op lowering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:290
msgid "3. The Other Paths"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:292
msgid ""
"Besides the fast path, the backend keeps two additional paths. They are "
"correct and tested, but they are not the current performance mainline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:295
msgid "3.1 Shared Cooperative Tensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:297
msgid ""
"If the frontend IR already contains shared staging, the backend lowers it as "
"a shared cooperative tensor path:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:300
msgid ""
"global A/B -> threadgroup A/B -> cooperative tensor operand -> MPP -> C\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:304
msgid ""
"This preserves the shape of CUDA-style kernels and is appropriate when "
"shared memory carries real semantics: layout transforms, padding or edge "
"zero-fill, multi-consumer reuse, threadgroup communication, or address "
"patterns that the direct-global path cannot currently express."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:309
msgid ""
"If shared memory is only staging, it is an extra copy plus barrier on Metal. "
"In the current measurements, it is slower than the direct-global path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:312
msgid "3.2 Simdgroup Fallback"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:314
msgid "The simdgroup path lowers GEMM to simdgroup matrix intrinsics:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:316
msgid ""
"threadgroup A/B -> simdgroup_load -> simdgroup_multiply_accumulate -> "
"simdgroup_store\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:320
msgid ""
"It is a compatibility path used when C is in `local.fragment` or `metal."
"simdgroup`, or when lowering-time cooperative tensor conditions are not met. "
"Compared with cooperative tensor, it behaves more like an explicit fragment "
"backend: the backend manages fragment layout, load/store, and accumulation/"
"store policy. It is therefore not the M5 / Metal 4 optimization mainline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:327
msgid "3.3 Why These Paths Are Kept"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:329
msgid "Existing TileLang kernels may already use CUDA-style staging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:330
msgid ""
"Shared staging may carry layout transform, padding, edge zero-fill, or multi-"
"consumer reuse semantics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:332
msgid ""
"Some non-contiguous or edge-heavy workloads cannot yet be expressed by the "
"direct-global path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler_internals/metal_tilelang_development.md:334
msgid ""
"Older Apple GPUs and non-Metal-4 runtimes need a complete simdgroup fallback "
